        {
          "id": "SP_CHAPERIA_GRANULOSA_GORDON_1986",
          "name": "Chaperia granulosa Gordon, 1986",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Chaperia",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Colony encrusting, multiserial; maximum colony size not known but, judging by specimens seen, certainly up to 10 mm or more; pale brown. Zooids variable in shape, moderately large, quincuncial, ranging from subquadrangular (diamond-shaped) to irregularly pentagonal, distal margin arcuate, raised, lateral margins typically diverging outwards proximally, mostly straight, proximal end truncate, concavely arcuate or V-shaped depending on position in colony; length: width ratio variable, longer than wide on average, but some zooids can be wider than long. Interzooidal boundaries marked by thin lines in moderately deep furrows. Cryptocystal frontal wall convex, rising to level of orificial rim, surface evenly granular, a narrow extension of cryptocyst around opesia distally, up to 4 granules in width between spine bases. ZL 502 ‒ 990 (714) μm, ZW 484 ‒ 852 (584) μm, n = 70. Mean ZL: ZW ratio 1.22. Opesia variable in length and width, mostly wider than long but in some zooids can be as long as wide, suboval to subcircular, the margin smooth and mostly narrow, a little wide in proximolateral corners. Frontal rims of occlusor laminae thin, curving gently toward distal oral rim without converging. Occlusor-muscle recesses longitudinally subcrescentic with pointed ends. OpL 234 ‒ 318 (271) μm, OpW 242 ‒ 361 (314) μm, n = 70. Mean OpL: ZL ratio 0.38.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:4985371"
